      "text": "# VU0 byte VMA 0x268: bounded static numerical evidence\n\nThis evidence accompanies the experimental model in `tools/vu/`. It contains numeric test output, exact source-span/LOI metadata, and Jev receipts. It deliberately excludes a full assembly listing, full decompiler output, or game payload bytes.\n\nThe PAL executable identity is SHA-256 `216711210898aee296eed73d0776e7f733bac04c334002683bce769c86beea95`. `parse_overlays` maps overlay 7 to VMA 0 at file offset `1162480`; the exact pair span `[77,102)` starts at `1163096`, is 200 bytes, and has SHA-256 `24fbedaf59f41ea50e1f3507e7ca7a2ad15642e22c7a05b3cd955576c4b83611`. The guard checks raw LOI payload words and the model bit table.\n\nThe host-side binary32 model uses exact raw LOI bits, rounds caller test values once to binary32 as QMTC2 payloads, then applies a toward-zero approximation only to arithmetic. Over 20,001 samples on `[0,2π]`, max absolute differences from host libm were `9.381821246406963e-7` (x vs sine) and `8.022761451842442e-7` (y vs cosine). Over `[-10,10]` the differences were `2.0470653239734737e-6` and `1.4899542371549224e-6`; over `[-100,100]`, `1.7534069339519842e-5` and `1.3138062233630787e-5`. Separate checks include 10,000 deterministic inputs, 51 quarter-turn boundary probes, lane invariance, a swapped-lane negative control, and a nearest-even rounding negative control.\n\nThese are static and host-model results only. They do not establish original programmer intent, arbitrary-input limits, exact PS2 silicon rounding, VU pipeline/flag/exception behavior, complete caller state, or runtime equivalence. Jev review receipts are advisory: the model review returned `review` with test-gap confidence limiting the result; the final combined promotion review escalated at safe-to-apply 0.62 because blast-ra"
